This fixture exercises phpc's deterministic placeholder
`mysqli_stmt_result_metadata()` and `mysqli_stmt_field_count()` support for
the current seed-post WordPress SELECT shape. System PHP requires a real
initialized MySQLi connection and prepared statement metadata; phpc only maps
the known placeholder query shape to deterministic field metadata and does not
implement prepared binding, execution, result rows, host database metadata,
PHP warning/error fidelity, or native database lowering.
